# world-holidays

Public holidays for every country, for the current and next year.
Zero runtime dependencies, fully typed.

```bash
npm i world-holidays
```

```ts
import { getHolidays, isHoliday, getNextHoliday, getWorldHolidays } from "world-holidays";

getHolidays("BD", 2027);          // [{ date: "2027-02-21", name: "..." }, ...]
isHoliday("US", "2026-12-25");    // { date: "2026-12-25", name: "Christmas Day" }
getNextHoliday("JP");             // next holiday from today
getWorldHolidays(2027);           // every country with its holidays
```

## API

| Function | Returns |
| --- | --- |
| `getCountries()` | `{ code, name }[]` |
| `getHolidays(code, year?)` | holidays of one country |
| `getWorldHolidays(year?)` | all countries with holidays |
| `getAllHolidaysFlat(year?)` | flat list, sorted by date |
| `isHoliday(code, date?)` | the holiday or `null` |
| `getNextHoliday(code, from?)` | the next holiday or `null` |
| `years`, `generatedAt` | coverage info |

## Notes

Dates are calculated from rules, not taken from government announcements.
Holidays based on moon sighting (for example Eid) can differ by a day.
Always verify critical dates against official sources.

